<div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px">
</div>
<div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px; --_image-block-width:300px;">
<img src="https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-2753/jenga.png" alt="jenga.png" class="image">
<div class="scp-image-caption">
<p>
T"Photo of SCP-2753-A instance taken during Boston Anomalous Art Expo (BAAE) prior to collapse."
</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>
<strong>
T"Item #:"
</strong>
T" SCP-2753"
</p>
<p>
<strong>
T"Object Class:"
</strong>
T" Keter"
</p>
<p>
<strong>
T"Special Containment Procedures:"
</strong>
T" A Foundation-operated bot ("
<a href="/scp-3089">
T"I/O-SILVER"
</a>
T") is to monitor internet traffic for SCP-2753. Upon discovery, all data containing SCP-2753 is to be destroyed. Anyone outside of Foundation personnel aware of SCP-2753 is to be apprehended, interrogated, and amnesticized."
</p>
<p>
T"Instances of SCP-2753-A are to be kept disassembled in a secure locker on-site. Instances of SCP-2753-B and SCP-2753-C are to be handled on a case-by-case basis. Tests are prohibited at this time."
</p>
<p>
<strong>
T"Description:"
</strong>
T" SCP-2753 is a 3 dimensional ratio that can be used to describe the relationship between the sides of a block."
</p>
<p>
T"Instances of SCP-2753-A are blocks which match SCP-2753's projection within a certain threshold; they can otherwise be of any size and material. They exhibit their anomalous property only when 42 instances of similar size and material are assembled into a standard Jenga"
<sup class="footnoteref">
<a id="footnoteref-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference(&#x27;footnote-1&#x27;)">
T"1"
</a>
</sup>
T" tower: If this tower collapses, any structure containing it will immediately collapse with it."
</p>
<p>
T"Since 2009, the growing popularity and accuracy of 3D printing combined with SCP-2753's presentation within OBJ files"
<sup class="footnoteref">
<a id="footnoteref-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference(&#x27;footnote-2&#x27;)">
T"2"
</a>
</sup>
T" as a printable Jenga set has led to 21 structural collapses, 35 injuries, and 14 deaths."
</p>
<p>
<strong>
T"Addendum 2753.1:"
</strong>
T" Incidents"
</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"► ACCESS SCP:/2753/incidents/007.log"
</a>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"▼ Close File"
</a>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p style="text-align: center;">
<strong>
T"INCIDENT LOG"
</strong>
</p>
<hr>
<p>
<strong>
T"DATE:"
</strong>
T" 1988/07/07"
<br>
T" "
<strong>
T"SUBJECT:"
</strong>
T" SCP-2753-A"
</p>
<hr>
<p>
T"The collapse of a warehouse used to host the Boston Anomalous Art Expo"
<sup class="footnoteref">
<a id="footnoteref-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference(&#x27;footnote-3&#x27;)">
T"3"
</a>
</sup>
T" was linked to an instance of SCP-2753-A. 14 additional anomalous objects (including "
<a href="/scp-1433">
T"SCP-1433"
</a>
T", an instance of "
<a href="/scp-1617">
T"SCP-1617"
</a>
T", and "
<a href="/project-proposal-1994-103">
T"SCP-████"
</a>
T") were also recovered amidst the wreckage. The collapse left over 49 participants injured and 21 dead. The following note was discovered nearby:"
</p>
<blockquote>
<p>
T"How High Can High Art Get? Let's Find Out!"
</p>
<p>
T"This tower is to be assembled at the start of the exposition; audience members are encouraged to take turns trying to take art higher and higher!"
</p>
<p>
T"But be warned: High art carries high risk! Reach too high, and you might just find your paradigm comes crashing down right on top of your head!"
</p>
<p>
T"- "
<a href="/are-we-cool-yet-hub">
T"AWCY"
</a>
</p>
</blockquote>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"► ACCESS SCP:/2753/incidents/021.log"
</a>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"▼ Close File"
</a>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p style="text-align: center;">
<strong>
T"INCIDENT LOG"
</strong>
</p>
<hr>
<p>
<strong>
T"DATE:"
</strong>
T" 1995/07/14"
<br>
T" "
<strong>
T"SUBJECT:"
</strong>
T" SCP-2753-B"
</p>
<hr>
<p>
T"Based on information provided by an undisclosed source, the Foundation-operated bot (I/O-SILVER) was used to search for SCP-2753 projections in financial market data. The collapse of several investment firms and multi-level marketing"
<sup class="footnoteref">
<a id="footnoteref-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference(&#x27;footnote-4&#x27;)">
T"4"
</a>
</sup>
T" companies were unexpectedly linked to SCP-2753."
</p>
<p>
T"Further investigation has demonstrated the existence of SCP-2753-B instances. Instances are financial assets that match SCP-2753's projection within a certain threshold; they can otherwise be of any value and type. They exhibit their anomalous property only when 42 instances of similar value and type are assembled into an interdependent network: If this network loses solvency, any corporate entity linked to it will experience an immediate catastrophic financial collapse."
</p>
<p>
T"Foundation efforts are currently underway to discover all such networks and safely disassemble them."
</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"► ACCESS SCP:/2753/incidents/035.log"
</a>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link">
<a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">
T"▼ Close File"
